From 8640b7a3037fb8f940df78f145701921d9903bdc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 11:38:21 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 03/15] Round 3: Rank dispatch contenders with one integer key

Store waiting starts in a dense array and precompute a tie-break tail
when a train becomes ready. Each contender's score maps to a total-order
integer and joins the tail in one u128, so ranking is an unsigned
maximum with the same (score, earlier wait, lower index) order. Unit
tests cover the key order against f64::total_cmp.

Workload: domain in matrix mode (48 candidates, 110 trains), 11 samples.
Before median: 1.958 ms. After median: 1.434 ms. Speedup: 1.37x.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
